On Fri, 1 Apr 2005, Felice aus Salum wrote:

> 1.) Is it possible to only sip at a potion before swallowing the
> whole?

No. It is possible to inhale the vapour of a potion, but it is used up
nevertheless, and you can identify only few potions this way.

> I'm thinking of testing for poison for example or already
> getting this typical mesage, that lets me guess, what this potion is.
> If not so: Is there a way of identifying potion without scroll of
> identify without swallowing or throwing at monsters?

Some potions can be identified by dipping certain objects into them. A
general way to identify all sorts of items is to ask shopkeepers for their
prices; of course, you would have to know the items' base prices for that
(see the spoilers at spod-central.org, were also the effects of dipping
are outlined).

> 2.) Is it possible to mix potions?

Yes, by dipping one into another. (This is commonly refered to as
"alchemy".) The effects range from comprehensible (healing+gain
energy=extra healing) to obscure (fruit juice+gain level=see invisible).

> I fell asleep every now and then, so
> I though, my character's tired and lay down in a corner and just
> waited (and sleept) for 50 turns. Then I went on, still falling asleep
> and the intervalls between shortend. Of cause I died after a while.
> Reading a few articles here, I found out that it was no natural
> sleepieness, but what was it?

You were wearing an amulet of restful sleep. Amulets can have very nasty
effects; it is wise to check whether you could take it off again before
trying an unidentified amulet.

